    { "key": "ui.summary.fact", "value": "Did you know? {fact}" },
    { "key": "day.1.fact", "value": "Atmospheric CO2 has risen about 50% since the Industrial Revolution, because we burn fossil fuels and cut down forests. As warming continues, hot extremes and heavy rain increase, and drought worsens in some regions." },
    { "key": "day.2.fact", "value": "Waste such as food and paper can release methane as it rots in landfills. Over 100 years, methane traps about 27-30 times more heat than the same amount of CO2. Recycling organic waste avoids this methane." },
    { "key": "day.3.fact", "value": "The last 11 years were the 11 hottest on record. Long-term warming has reached about 1.4°C above pre-industrial levels. If it continues, wildfire weather increases in many regions, and heat and drought deepen crop losses." },
    { "key": "day.4.fact", "value": "Oceans absorb about 90% of the extra heat. The price is high: warming water expands, sea levels rise, corals bleach and a greater share of tropical cyclones become intense." },
    { "key": "day.5.fact", "value": "In 2024 the average person faced 16 days of dangerous heat that would not have been expected without climate change. The heat-related death rate is up 23% since the 1990s." },
